{"Title":"Northborough select board","BillNumber":"S2495","DocketNumber":null,"GeneralCourtNumber":193,"PrimarySponsor":{"Id":"RKK0","Name":"Robyn K. Kennedy","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/RKK0","ResponseDate":"2023-11-01T09:36:44.543"},"Cosponsors":[{"Id":"RKK0","Name":"Robyn K. Kennedy","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/RKK0","ResponseDate":"2023-11-01T09:36:44.5566667"}],"JointSponsor":null,"BillHistory":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Documents/S2495/DocumentHistoryActions","LegislationTypeName":"Amendment","Pinslip":"Senate, December 18, 2023  - Text of the Senate amendment (Senator R. Kennedy) to the House Bill relative to the select board of the town of Northborough (House, No. 3902).","DocumentText":"\tSECTION 1. Notwithstanding any general or special law to the contrary, the executive body of the town of Northborough, previously known as the board of selectmen, shall be known as the select board and shall have the powers and authority of a board of selectmen under any general or special law and the members of the select board, previously known as selectmen, shall be known as select board members. \r\n\tSECTION 2. Notwithstanding sections 21 and 32 of chapter 40 of the General Laws, section 5 of chapter 40A of the General Laws, or any other general or special law to the contrary, the select board of the town of Northborough may amend the general by-laws and zoning by-laws of the town by majority vote to revise all references to the board of selectmen and selectmen to the select board and select board members, respectively, in accordance with section 1. \r\n\tSECTION 3. This act shall take effect upon its passage.\r\n","EmergencyPreamble":null,"RollCalls":[],"Attachments":[],"CommitteeRecommendations":[],"Amendments":[]}